# Build context for the Cloud Run image (Dockerfile in this directory).
#
# This file is ALSO passed to `gcloud builds submit --ignore-file=.dockerignore`, so it decides
# what gets uploaded to Cloud Build as well as what `docker build` can see. Two consequences:
#
#   * Dockerfile and .dockerignore are deliberately NOT excluded. Docker reads the Dockerfile
#     out of band, but Cloud Build reads it from the uploaded tarball — exclude it here and the
#     build fails with "Dockerfile not found" and no obvious cause.
#   * Excluding a path here means the source tarball never leaves the machine with it. That is
#     the point for outputs/ (deployment records) and data/ (must not exist at all — see
#     .gitignore).

node_modules/
npm-debug.log
*.log

# Deploy records written by the deploy scripts. Never part of an image.
outputs/

# .gitignore forbids this directory existing: every source is live, there is no offline index.
# Belt and braces so a stray local copy can never be baked into a public image.
data/

.git/
.gitignore

# 40KB of integrator documentation. Useful in the repo, dead weight in a container.
README.md

# Deploy tooling — shell scripts that run on an operator's machine, not in the container.
scripts/gcp-vm/
scripts/cloudrun/

# The unit suite (306 tests) runs from the source tree via `npm test`, never from the image.
# NOTE: if a future Dockerfile ever adds a `RUN npm test` gate, remove this line first — with
# it in place the tests are simply absent and the gate would pass green on nothing.
scripts/lib/*.test.mjs
